From 5c1b127c839f84d6182265714bf43338e654b3d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-ID: <5c1b127c839f84d6182265714bf43338e654b3d6.1794484962.git.jdenemar@redhat.com>
From: Michal Privoznik <mprivozn@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:46:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Model qemuInterfaceOpenVhostNet() mock more closely to
 its source

Inside of qemuxml2argvmock.c there's an alternative
implementation of qemuInterfaceOpenVhostNet(). Fair enough. But
the original function (living in qemu_interface.c) has a check
which exits early from the function. This check is lacking in the
mock which then leads qemuxmlconftest generate a different cmd
line than the production code.

The is particularly important, when the check is changed and we
want to verify through tests that it doesn't break anything.

Signed-off-by: Michal Privoznik <mprivozn@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Martin Kletzander <mkletzan@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6e1a9eae6ed34cc3b902f5c6e7379a2aa5d002fc)

Conflicts:
tests/qemuxmlconfdata/downscript.x86_64-latest.args
tests/qemuxmlconfdata/net-coalesce.x86_64-latest.args
